# Smallest Governance Program

This runnable candidate is deterministically instantiated from the DomainSpec
project in [`domainspec/`](domainspec/). The closed instantiation profile binds
the Governance language to accepted Rust realizations from DomainSpec baseline
`{{BASELINE_ID}}` (`{{BASELINE_DIGEST}}`).

```text
Governance Program + Governance Request + Governance Fact Set
                              |
                              v
                    pure evaluate Calculation
                              |
                              v
                 allow | deny | abstain | error
```

The default scenario omits the active-binding Fact and therefore returns
`abstain`. Missing governance authority or applicability is neither permission
nor prohibition.

## Generate and check exact bytes

From the repository root, using the pinned DomainSpec Node toolchain:

```bash
toolchains/node-typescript/bin/node-env run \
  --project projects/domainspec-v2/impl/cli -- \
  node tools/governance-kernel.mjs generate \
  /workspace/cyberAlchemy-v2/development/examples/smallest-governance-program/domainspec \
  /workspace/cyberAlchemy-v2/development/examples/smallest-governance-program

toolchains/node-typescript/bin/node-env run \
  --project projects/domainspec-v2/impl/cli -- \
  node tools/governance-kernel.mjs check \
  /workspace/cyberAlchemy-v2/development/examples/smallest-governance-program/domainspec \
  /workspace/cyberAlchemy-v2/development/examples/smallest-governance-program
```

